  "summary": "A side channel (regenerative) blower has an impeller with many blades running past a ring-shaped channel in the housing. Air enters, is flung outward by the blades into the side channel, flows back to the blade roots and is picked up again — many times around one revolution. This helical regeneration builds pressure like a multistage machine, oil-free and almost pulsation-free.",
